# ARA Fiscal Model

Produces every number in Part VI (Economic Feasibility) of the American Renewal Agenda.

## Files
- `ara_fiscal_inputs.json` â€” every amount, adjustment factor, growth rate, timing assumption, uncertainty rating and source number (Part XI register). Edit this file, not the code.
- `fiscal_model.py` â€” the model: year-by-year profiles FY2027â€“2039, CBO-style debt service, scenario totals, sensitivities, and a 20,000-draw simulation.
- `gen_part6.py` â€” writes Part VI (`out/part6.md`) and the chart data (`out/chart.json`) from the model.
- `out/` â€” `ledger.csv`, `annual_central.csv`, `summary.json`, `ARA_FiscalModel_2026.xlsx`.

## Run
    pip install numpy scipy openpyxl
    python3 fiscal_model.py     # tables to out/
    python3 gen_part6.py        # Part VI text and chart data

## Conventions
- Billions of nominal dollars; positive = adds to the deficit.
- Window FY2030â€“2039 (Phase I bills enacted 2029); FY2027â€“2036 view also reported.
- Older estimates: annual = total / years Ã— factors Ã— (1 + g)^(year âˆ’ source midpoint) Ã— ramp.
- Debt service: r Ã— (cumulative added debt through tâˆ’1 + Â½ Ã— deficit change in t), compounding, r = 3.9%.
- Revenue stacking: IRS â†’ loopholes â†’ wealth tax (Ã—0.9) â†’ public option. Wealth tax legal-risk weight 0.5.
- Simulation: triangular per line; correlated groups (revenue execution 0.6, take-up 0.5); seed 2028.

endstream
endobj
