A(f"Three results stand out. The Medicare offsets are the largest single protection: without them the agenda would add {T(MEDX)}. Family take-up is the largest cost uncertainty. And because the Phase II family programs are paced by Phase II revenue, a court loss on the billionaire income tax mostly slows those programs instead of adding to the deficit; the bill also keeps its deferral charge and tax at death if the annual inclusion is struck down (BWDS Sec. 204(f)), and with only that fallback the ten-year effect is {T(BTD)}. Interest rates matter more for the baseline than for this agenda: 0.5 point higher adds {T(sens_d['Interest rates 0.5 point higher than assumed']-FC['total'])} to the agenda\'s own interest cost, but $1.9 trillion to the nation\'s, which is why revenue comes first in the sequence.")
