   "uncertainty": "Very high",
   "unc_detail": "Data M Â· Model H Â· Behaviour H Â· Legal M",
   "basis": "The bill taxes billionaires' gains each year as income (mark-to-market on traded assets, a deferral charge on other assets, and tax at death), the design JCT scored at $557B over 2022â€“2031 [930]; Penn Wharton found $507B [931]. Reduced 10% for overlap with the loophole closures, grown 4% a year, and weighted for legal risk at even odds, since four Justices in Moore signaled that realization is required: if a court strikes the annual inclusion, Sec. 204(f) keeps the deferral charge and tax at death, assumed to keep 40% of revenue within the window. Low: fallback only. High: upheld, with a rate above the capital gains rate.",
